  sections:
  - SectionName: Room  Configuration
    Questions:
    - QuestionText: There are clearly defined patient, family, and caregiver zones
        within the room.
      IsAnsweredCorrectly: 0
    - QuestionText: There is sufficient space for caregivers to provide care around
        the patient bed.
      IsAnsweredCorrectly: 1
    - QuestionText: The room has sufficient clearance for wheelchairs, furniture,
        and medical equipment.
      IsAnsweredCorrectly: 1
    - QuestionText: All elements in the rooms are located and oriented uniformly
        to allow standardization of care processes.
      IsAnsweredCorrectly: 1
    - QuestionText: There is sufficient space in the room to accommodate mobile equipment
        including patient handling equipment.
      IsAnsweredCorrectly: 1
    - QuestionText: There is s ufficient space and provision for equipment, medical
        gases, and power capacity to accommodate different levels of patient acuity
        including codes.
      IsAnsweredCorrectly: 1
    - QuestionText: Overall, the room layout enables patient (and family) mobility
        within the room and to/from the corridor.
      IsAnsweredCorrectly: 1
  - SectionName: Accessibility & Safety
    Questions:
    - QuestionText: There is clear, barrier - free access to the bathroom.
      IsAnsweredCorrectly: 1
    - QuestionText: There is a supported path (e.g. handrail) to bathroom.
      IsAnsweredCorrectly: 0
    - QuestionText: The bathroom door is large door openings to accommodate patients,
        equipment, and caregivers.
      IsAnsweredCorrectly: 1
    - QuestionText: The bathroom door opening direction meets patient room design
        criteria (By researcher).
      IsAnsweredCorrectly: 0
    - QuestionText: There is sufficient clearance between the bed and chair for a
        pivot - turn transfer for a wheelchair.
      IsAnsweredCorrectly: 1
    - QuestionText: There are standing assist aids/lifts with ambulation capacity.
      IsAnsweredCorrectly: 1
    - QuestionText: There are no sharp edges in furniture, fixtures, equipment that
        could cause injury to patient/staff.
      IsAnsweredCorrectly: 1
    - QuestionText: Medication Safety Zones (MSZ) identified within the patient room.
      IsAnsweredCorrectly: 0
    - QuestionText: Storage areas are clearly labeled to improve work efficiency.
      IsAnsweredCorrectly: 0
    - QuestionText: Design supports handwashing compliance.
      IsAnsweredCorrectly: 1
    - QuestionText: Design supports hand sanitization.
      IsAnsweredCorrectly: 0
    - QuestionText: Visual cues as reminder for hand washing/sanitization.
      IsAnsweredCorrectly: 0
    - QuestionText: There is sufficient illumination for caregivers to provide care
        around the patient bed.
      IsAnsweredCorrectly: 1
    - QuestionText: Patient has access to daylight and sunlight without compromising
        visual comfort.
      IsAnsweredCorrectly: 1
    - QuestionText: Patient has access to views of nature and other positive distractions.
      IsAnsweredCorrectly: 1
  - SectionName: Visibility of Patient, Monitors, Supplies, and/or Equipment
    Questions:
    - QuestionText: Patient visible to staff as they enter the room.
      IsAnsweredCorrectly: 1
    - QuestionText: Storage & supplies visible to staff.
      IsAnsweredCorrectly: 1
    - QuestionText: Monitors and Medical equipment visible to staff.
      IsAnsweredCorrectly: 1
    - QuestionText: Handwashing sinks visible to staff as they enter the room.
      IsAnsweredCorrectly: 0
    - QuestionText: Alcohol gel dispensers in visible and accessible locations.
      IsAnsweredCorrectly: 1
    - QuestionText: The bathroom door is visible to the patient while in bed.
      IsAnsweredCorrectly: 1
    - QuestionText: Design supports visual privacy.
      IsAnsweredCorrectly: 0
  - SectionName: Aesthetics & Ambiance
    Questions:
    - QuestionText: Patient room layout satisfies the needs of staff when working
        in the room.
      IsAnsweredCorrectly: 1
    - QuestionText: The overall ambient environment of the patient room (including
        staff wor k zone) appears attractive and pleasant to staff.
      IsAnsweredCorrectly: 1
  - SectionName: Storage & Supplies
    Questions:
    - QuestionText: There is accessible and well organized, storage for common medical
        supplies.
      IsAnsweredCorrectly: 1
    - QuestionText: There is adequate space for storage of personal belongings.
      IsAnsweredCorrectly: 0
